<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrios Ypsilantis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1832</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrios Ypsilantis was a Greek army officer of the War of Independence from a Phanariot family; his brother Alexandros led the rising of 1821 in the Danubian Principalities. Arriving in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in June 1821 as his brother's representative, he claimed the national leadership and clashed with the local notables. He took part in the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli-greece">Tripolitsa</a>, defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> in 1822 and in 1829 commanded the Greek army in the war's last battle, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petra">Petra</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demetrios-ypsilantis.jpg" alt="Demetrios Ypsilantis" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spyridon Prosalentis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dimitrios_Ypsilantis_-_Sp._Prosalentis.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
